  "_comment": [
    "Twenty-five across as written, so `colossal` is a hundred.",
    "**Two or three ellipsoids stuck together, and three such lumps to draw from.** One ellipsoid roughened",
    "by a noise is still an ellipsoid: the silhouette gives it away however hard the surface is worked. Off",
    "-centre lobes are what break the outline, and the list is what makes one boulder differ from the next --",
    "a copy draws one entry, then a yaw and a size, so three lumps by eight turns by three sizes is what the",
    "eye actually meets.",
    "The undulation is heavier than it was (amount 1.5 -> 3.5, three octaves) because a bigger rock needs a",
    "coarser surface to read as rock at all."
